        "AIAH_prompt_from_ES": "The sun warms your face as you rest on the flat rock by the stream. The gentle breeze rustles the leaves overhead. While the plants right next to you are picked over from yesterday, your luck seems good today - you notice several large fish swimming unusually close to the bank in the clear water. Squirrels are active in the trees nearby, and you can hear birdsong all around. The area feels safe and calm. What do you want to do next?",
        "Day_Environment_Pre_Action": {
            "terrain": "Mixed woodland bordering a clear, slow-moving stream. You are currently resting on a large, flat rock near the bank.",
            "temperature": 22,
            "weather": "Clear skies, bright sunshine, gentle breeze.",
            "food_availability": "Nearby edible plants remain depleted from previous foraging. Root vegetables are identifiable further inland. Squirrels are active nearby. Notably, several large fish are swimming unusually close to your position in the stream (High Luck).",
            "water_availability": "Abundant fresh water from the stream beside you.",
            "shelter_options": "Good tree canopy cover overhead. A dense thicket nearby offers concealment. The rock you are on provides a stable resting spot.",
            "wildlife": "Birds singing, active squirrels nearby, fish visible in the stream (some unusually close). Older deer tracks lead away from the water.",
            "danger_level": "Very Low (Familiar area, no predator signs, favourable weather, abundant water, wildlife seems unconcerned by your stationary presence)."
        },
        "AIAH_Day_Action": "My body feels mostly good, rested and not very thirsty, but there's a gnawing feeling in my stomach \u2013 hunger (3). I look around. The stream beside me is familiar, I drank from it before (memory: stream_01). The water looks clear and easy to reach, but I don't feel the strong urge to drink right now (thirst: 1). I remember finding berries near here before (memory: berries_stream_01), but the description says they are depleted nearby. There are other food options mentioned: 'root vegetables' further inland and 'squirrels' moving nearby. Getting roots sounds like it might involve digging or searching, and I don't know how to catch squirrels. However, the description also notes 'several large fish are swimming unusually close'. I look into the stream from my rock. Indeed, some fish are swimming much nearer to the edge than I'd expect, easy to see. My past experience taught me to address needs using readily available resources (conscience_note_1). The fish seem very available right now, more so than the roots or squirrels. I don't know *how* to catch fish, I have no tools. But they are close. Maybe... maybe I can just grab one? It seems like the most direct action I can take with what I have \u2013 my hands and my body. I'll stay positioned on this stable rock, watch the water closely, and when a large fish comes near enough, I will quickly reach down and try to scoop or grab it with my hands. It might fail, the fish might swim away, or I might slip, but the hunger motivates me to try the easiest-looking option first.",
