            "water_availability": "Clear, fresh water easily accessible from the stream. Negligible change from agent drinking.",
            "shelter_options": "Thick tree canopy provides good cover overhead. The large, flat rock is currently occupied by the agent. A dense thicket a short distance away offers concealment.",
            "wildlife": "Birdsong continues, adapting to the progressing morning. Squirrels chatter occasionally, keeping their distance from the stationary agent. Fish dart in the stream. The deer tracks on the trail appear slightly less fresh than at dawn.",
            "danger_level": "Low (Familiar location, agent is stationary and non-threatening, favorable weather, ample water, no predator signs detected. Wildlife remains cautious but unalarmed.)",
            "notes_for_future": {
                "wildlife_alert": "Agent's stationary presence on the rock continues. Nearby small wildlife (squirrels, birds) maintain cautious distance but show no increased alarm. Wildlife activity patterns shifting naturally as morning progresses.",
                "resource_change": "Agent consumed a small amount of water (negligible impact). No food resources gathered. Previously depleted food patches near the stream show no recovery yet.",
