        "Day_Environment_Post_Action": {
            "terrain": "Mixed woodland bordering a clear, slow-moving stream. The large, flat rock near the stream bank is now marked with fish scales, blood, and discarded fish guts. A suitable sharp-edged rock lies nearby. Signs of previous foraging remain visible further along the bank.",
            "temperature": 25,
            "weather": "Clear skies, warm sunshine persists, gentle breeze (slightly carrying the scent of fish).",
            "food_availability": "One portion of prepared raw fish meat (gutted and scaled). Fish waste (guts, scales) is present on the flat rock. Nearby edible plants remain depleted. Root vegetables identifiable further inland. Squirrels remain wary and distant.",
            "water_availability": "Abundant fresh water from the stream (agent drank some, negligible impact).",
            "shelter_options": "Good tree canopy overhead. A dense thicket nearby offers concealment. The large, flat rock is functional but now messy and scented.",
            "wildlife": "Birds cautiously active at a distance. Squirrels remain wary and further away, potentially chattering in response to the smell. Stream fish remain in deeper water. Insects (flies) beginning to investigate the fish waste. The scent may attract other scavengers or predators over time.",
            "danger_level": "Low-Medium. While no immediate threats are visible (high luck), the strong scent of fish blood and waste significantly increases the likelihood of attracting scavengers (flies already present) and potentially larger predators to the location in the near future. Risk of raw fish spoilage remains.",
            "notes_for_future": {
