                "context": "Low energy (6) and persistent illness (3), though slightly improved from before. Aware that easily accessible food resources near the stream were depleted by previous actions (as noted in prior reflection). In a familiar, low-danger location.",
                "reflection": "Successfully applied previous lessons regarding the importance of rest for energy conservation when health is compromised and the reality of local resource depletion. The conscious decision to prioritize rest and observation over immediate foraging, despite rising hunger (now 3), demonstrates strategic thinking and adaptation based on self-assessment (low energy/illness) and environmental awareness (depleted resources). This reinforces the value of patience and observation as survival tools.",
                "emotional_response": {
