        "AIAH_Day_Action": "My body feels rested (sleep score 10), yet my energy is very low (3) and I still feel unwell (illness 4). My hunger and thirst are low (2 and 1). The most striking things here are the strong smell of fish waste coming from the flat rock I remember using before, and the flies buzzing around it. The rock is stained and looks unclean now. There's prepared fish nearby, but it looks different, maybe less fresh than before, and the description mentions 'spoilage'. My diary reminds me that resting is crucial when energy is low and I'm unwell (Conscience Note 1 & 2), and that untreated things can be risky (Conscience Note 2). Eating the spoiling fish seems like a bad idea, especially when I'm already ill. The smell is also concerning; the environment update notes it increases the risk of attracting unwanted attention. My energy is too low (3) to try foraging for the root vegetables further inland, which sounds like hard work, and the plants near the stream are depleted anyway (Memory Day 3, Environment Update). The flat rock is no longer a good place to rest due to the contamination and smell. Therefore, my priority must be to conserve my limited energy while minimizing risk. I will first drink some fresh water from the stream, being careful to take it from a spot away from the waste on the rock if possible. Then, I will move a short distance away from the smelly, contaminated flat rock and the spoiling fish, perhaps finding a spot under the shade of the trees closer to the dense thicket I remember seeing (Memory - thicket_01), but not so far that it uses too much energy. Resting there will help conserve energy, which my diary indicates is very important right now. From this new resting spot, I will observe my surroundings carefully, watching for any animals attracted by the fish smell and keeping an eye on the area where the root vegetables were mentioned.",
