                "lesson_learned": "Processing animal resources requires tools/skills and generates waste. This waste *actively* attracts pests and predators, significantly increasing local danger, as previously theorized and now potentially observed. Ignoring or remaining near waste is highly risky, especially when vulnerable (e.g., low energy, illness). Mitigation (moving away, potentially disposal/burial if feasible) is crucial. Validating environmental cues (smell, insects, sounds) against learned risks enables timely, preventative action and confirms the importance of waste management."
            }
