        },
        "AIAH_Day_Action": "My body feels reasonably rested (sleep 10), and my immediate hunger (2) and thirst (1) are low. However, my memory (fish_waste_01, flat_rock_01) and conscience notes (conscience_note_3) are very clear about the danger nearby. The decaying matter on the flat rock smells bad, attracts flies, and I learned this could attract dangerous animals. My illness (3) hasn't gone away completely, and staying near contamination feels risky (Risk Assessment skill). The breeze sometimes carries the bad smell right to me. My priority must be safety and avoiding known hazards (Hazard Avoidance skill). Therefore, I will carefully get up from my current resting spot under the trees. I need to move further away from the contaminated flat rock by the stream. I will try to move quietly and stay under the trees for cover, perhaps going slightly further into the woodland or moving upstream along the stream bank, away from the source of the smell and the flies. This uses some energy (currently 5), but avoiding the hazard feels more important right now, especially as my conscience diary emphasizes the danger of waste. I will keep observing my surroundings as I move. Once I find a suitable spot away from the immediate contamination, I will rest again and reassess.",
        "AIAH_Day_Action_Possibility": "possible",
