                        "caution": "Ongoing due to illness and potential nearby threat.",
                        "relief": "Distancing from immediate contamination/smell.",
                        "mild_anxiety": "Rustling sounds confirming potential danger."
                    },
                    "Reinforcement_2": {
                        "prudence": "Acting decisively on a known risk based on past experience.",
                        "relief": "Increased sense of safety and reduced immediate sensory discomfort (smell) after moving.",
                        "satisfaction": "Confirmation of learning and applying lessons effectively."
                    }
                },
                "lesson_learned": "Processing animal resources creates significant waste that actively attracts pests and predators, increasing local danger. This isn't just a theory; it's an observed reality. Ignoring or remaining near such waste is highly risky, especially when vulnerable. Proactive mitigation, specifically physical distancing/relocation from the hazard source, is an essential survival tactic, even if it requires energy expenditure. Trusting environmental cues (smell, insects) and memories of past consequences allows for timely, preventative action."
            }
